<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arsenio Martínez Campos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a>–<a href="/years/1900">1900</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arsenio Martínez Campos was a Spanish general who suppressed the cantonal rising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in 1873 and in December 1874 proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii">Alfonso XII</a> king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagunto">Sagunto</a>, restoring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> monarchy. He later ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-zanjon">Pact of Zanjón</a> in 1878 and served briefly as prime minister in 1879.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arsenio-martinez-campos.jpg" alt="Arsenio Martínez Campos" width="320" height="505" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Federico de Madrazo y Kuntz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Arsenio_Mart%C3%ADnez_Campos_(1831-1900).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
